<Layout title="new room new room" description="i have a new room and its a mess">
	<p class="date">mar 10, 2025</p>
	<p>Ignore how I said I was going to write about moving here lol, i kinda forgot...<p>
	<div class="sidecomp"><a href="/images/101.jpg"><img src="/images/101.jpg" alt="a clothing line strung through the middle of the room over the lamp"></a><span>chaos</span></div><p>
	I think I moved over most of my stuff two weeks ago but that doesn't mean theres any less chaos here now. The girl who lived here before thankfully left me a bunch of stuff, but most of it is very impractical so that I barely have any space to put stuff apart from the floor. My dad helped me put in a desk at least, but that barely helped... </p>
	<div class="sidecomp"><a href="/images/100.jpg"><img src="/images/100.jpg" alt="a small kitchen"></a><span>the kitchen</span></div><p>
	<p>So far I don't even have a chair, barely even the space for one. I've been thinking though, it might be cool to just have a big armchair there, but I'll see what I can find for cheap. Recently I've been seeing a bunch of very green rooms on pinterest so I'm planning to get a bunch of plants, that entire hobby seems crazy tho, so I have a lot of reading up to do before anything in that regard can happen. The flower seeds I got from a friend are sprouting now tho!! The walls here also seem like a very nice chance to get some new posters and stickers, or maybe some grafitti, altough I heard it's supposed to be very smelly.</p>
	<p>One thing noone told me about tho was how fucking expensive living on your own is. The ammount of random shit you suddenly need is insane n I can barely afford anything rn, so doing any decorating is put on hold until thats all figured out.</p>
	<p>I really don't want to complain though, living near the city centre is literally changing my entire life here, cuz I suddenly don't need a one hour heads up on everything anymore and being able to do stuff without having to think about moving again soon is great.</p>
</Layout>
